SUMMARY:Meet the Keepers
DESCRIPTION:Plan your visit to include a stop in the Charlotte Brody Discovery Garden for this special opportunity to meet the keepers of the bees\, chickens and incredible edible plants in this garden area beloved by learners of all ages. Look for horticulture staff or volunteers in Duke Gardens shirts and feel free to ask what they are doing.  Drop-in activity for all ages. Adult chaperone required for minors. \nFee: Free; no registration required. \nParking: Parking fees apply. \nLocation: Charlotte Brody Discovery Garden \nAccessibility: This is a drop-in program that takes place in an outdoor location that requires traveling on a combination of paved and unpaved paths with some uneven surfaces and moderate inclines.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/meet-the-keepers-14/
LOCATION:Duke Gardens – Charlotte Brody Discovery Garden\, 420 Anderson Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27708\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs,Family programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/Growing-2024-Transformations-AFTER-Charlotte-Brody-Discovery-Garden-Bill-Snead-Duke-Photography-2024.jpg
END:VEVENT
