SUMMARY:Build a Bug Snug
DESCRIPTION:Support winter wildlife and re-purpose garden cuttings with a bug snug\, an easy-to-make sculptural structure made of twigs and stems that provides a place for insects and invertebrates to overwinter.  Participants will work with Brooks Burleson\, artisan and owner of Natural Stone Installation\, to make a functional and attractive two-foot-tall structure to take home for your yard or garden. All materials provided. \nFee: $36; 20% discount for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nParking: Parking fees apply. \nLocation: Meet at the Barnes Welcome Center. \nAccessibility: This program takes place in an indoor location accessible via paved surfaces and equipped with a hearing loop\, which transmits sound directly to hearing aids and cochlear implants with a T-coil setting. Accessible restrooms are available onsite.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/build-a-bug-snug/
LOCATION:Duke Gardens–Barnes Welcome Center\, 420 Anderson Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27705\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/bug-snug-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
